{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:KnotsParticlesConfinement.ElectroweakTripletChargeSpinFromInvolution","@type":"LeanModule","name":"KnotsParticlesConfinement.ElectroweakTripletChargeSpinFromInvolution","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":95,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.label_forced_given_group_assignment","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.label_forced_given_group_assignment","kind":"theorem","line":745,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L745-L768","doc":"**The W/Z label IS forced, given the group assignment (§3b-cond conditional\npositive; answers \"can you prove it?\").** No single-slot topological invariant\nforces which slot is the charged `W`\n(`named_second_charge_candidates_do_not_force_label`, `signed_which_slot_is_W_free`),\nbut the `su(2)_L × u(1)_Y` group datum `EWGroupAssignment` DOES: the neutral\n`W³→Z` slot is the Cartan slot (`2·T₃ = 0`), the charged `W±` slot is the\ncomplementary root slot (`2·T₃ = 2`), and a slot is neutral **iff** it is the\nCartan slot — each DERIVED from the group assignment via the adjoint\nzero-weight rule (`derivedDoubledT3`), not projected. The label is determined:\nthe charged slot is exactly the non-Cartan slot. This relocates the postulate\nfrom a bare `T₃` label to the group-structure (mixing) input — it does not\nfabricate a topological forcing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.derivedDoubledT3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.derivedDoubledT3","kind":"def","line":737,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L737-L743","doc":"**Derived doubled isospin `2·T₃` from the group assignment.** The neutral\nCartan member `W³` sits in the **zero-weight** space of the `su(2)_L` adjoint, so\n`T₃ = 0`; the complementary root member `W±` has `|T₃| = 1` (`2·T₃` magnitude\n`2`). These are the adjoint weights `{+1, 0, −1}`, applied to the group datum — a\nderivation, not a re-postulation of `T₃`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWGroupAssignment.cartan_ne_charged","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWGroupAssignment.cartan_ne_charged","kind":"theorem","line":735,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L735-L735","doc":"The Cartan (neutral) and root (charged) slots are distinct — the\nnon-degeneracy of the Cartan–Weyl split of the adjoint triplet. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWGroupAssignment.chargedSlot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWGroupAssignment.chargedSlot","kind":"def","line":732,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L732-L732","doc":"Which vector slot hosts the charged `W±` root member. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWGroupAssignment.cartanSlot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWGroupAssignment.cartanSlot","kind":"def","line":730,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L730-L730","doc":"Which vector slot hosts the neutral `su(2)_L` Cartan member `W³` (→ `Z`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWGroupAssignment.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWGroupAssignment.mk","kind":"ctor","line":728,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L728-L728","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWGroupAssignment","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWGroupAssignment","kind":"class","line":719,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L719-L735","doc":"**The group-assignment datum (open §3b hypothesis class).** The genuine input\nthe topological invariants cannot supply: the alignment of the two vector slots\nwith the `su(2)_L` Cartan–Weyl basis. The fields carry WHICH slot is the neutral\n`su(2)_L` Cartan generator `W³` (→ `Z`) versus the charged `W±` root member —\na group-theoretic datum, NOT the `T₃` values (those are derived below). The\n`cartan_ne_charged` field is the genuine non-degeneracy of the Cartan–Weyl split\nof the adjoint triplet (exactly one neutral Cartan direction, complementary root).\nNo instance is provided; it is the open `(W³,B)→(Z,γ)` mixing input of\n`conj:weinberg-angle-categorical`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.instDecidableEqVectorSlot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.instDecidableEqVectorSlot","kind":"instance","line":717,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L717-L717","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.VectorSlot.s6","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.VectorSlot.s6","kind":"ctor","line":716,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L716-L716","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.VectorSlot.s4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.VectorSlot.s4","kind":"ctor","line":715,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L715-L715","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.VectorSlot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.VectorSlot","kind":"inductive","line":712,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L712-L717","doc":"The two `A₋` vector slots (crossing counts `4` and `6`) hosting the charged\n`W±` and the neutral `W³/Z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.named_second_charge_candidates_do_not_force_label","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.named_second_charge_candidates_do_not_force_label","kind":"theorem","line":679,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L679-L698","doc":"**The named second-charge candidates do NOT force the label.** The forcing\nhypothesis of `second_charge_would_force_neutral_slot` demands a charge that is\nzero on one vector slot and nonzero on the other. Neither candidate qualifies:\n\n* the Milnor triple linking `μ̄(123) ≡ 0` on **every** even-twist carrier (a\n  2-component link has no triple) — it vanishes on BOTH slots, so it produces no\n  charged slot;\n* the pairwise linking `Lk(T(2,2k)) = k ≠ 0` on **every** carrier (`k = 2,3,4`) —\n  it vanishes on NEITHER slot, so it produces no neutral slot.\n\nBoth halves do real work (`rfl`-per-`k` / `decide`), not a vacuous ¬∃: one\nexhibits a charge that is identically zero, the other a charge that is nowhere\nzero — the two distinct ways of missing the \"nonzero on exactly one slot\" datum\nthat `second_charge_would_force_neutral_slot` requires. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.evenTwistTripleLinking","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.evenTwistTripleLinking","kind":"def","line":672,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L672-L677","doc":"Milnor triple linking number `μ̄(123)` of the even-twist carrier. `T(2,2k)` is\na **two**-component link, and the triple linking number requires **≥ 3**\ncomponents, so it vanishes identically. Models the baryon / color-trace charge the\nU(1)-assignment audit names (`docs/audits/2026-06-02-u1-hypercharge-assignment.md`;\ncf. the three-strand color structure of `observations/hadron-proton-example`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.evenTwistLinkingNumber","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.evenTwistLinkingNumber","kind":"def","line":667,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L667-L670","doc":"Pairwise linking number of the even-twist carrier `T(2,2k)`: the two strands\nof the `(2,2k)` torus link wind `k` times, so `lk(T(2,2k)) = k`. Models the\ncategorical linking operation `Lk_R` (`conj:categorical-linking-operation`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.signed_C_does_not_force_W_slot_but_forces_neutral_mixed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.signed_C_does_not_force_W_slot_but_forces_neutral_mixed","kind":"theorem","line":628,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L628-L655","doc":"**Capstone (honest stronger negative).** Neither ingredient the prior result\nnamed forces which pure even-twist slot hosts the charged `W`:\n\n* the **signed `σ ↔ σ⁻¹` asymmetry** leaves ≥ 2 C-consistent labelings — two\n  distinct labelings disagree on the `W` slot (`signedWat4 ≠ signedWat6`, and\n  `sw 4` differs);\n* the neutrality criterion **is** C-invariance ⟺ amphichirality (`∀ w, −w = w ↔\n  w = 0`), and **no pure even-twist carrier is amphichiral** — all three carriers\n  `σ₁⁴` (k=2), `σ₃⁶` (k=3), `σ₅⁸` (k=4) are chiral — so the neutral electroweak\n  boson is *necessarily not a single even-twist slot* but the **mixed `W³/B → Z`\n  (Weinberg) state**.\n\nHence which-slot-is-`W` is fixed **only by the mixing / combination data**, not by\nany single-slot topological invariant — strengthening `which_slot_is_W_free` with\nthe *reason*: the correct neutrality criterion (charge-conjugation invariance)\nexcludes every chiral slot from being neutral. The remaining tie-breaker, a second\nbaryon/color-trace charge (`second_charge_would_force_neutral_slot`), is a missing\ncorpus object, not supplied. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.second_charge_would_force_neutral_slot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.second_charge_would_force_neutral_slot","kind":"theorem","line":609,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L609-L626","doc":"**What WOULD force the label: a second charge nonzero on exactly one slot.** If\na hypothetical second (baryon/color-trace) charge `S : ℕ → ℤ` vanishes on one\nvector slot and is nonzero on the other — reading \"neutral ⟺ `S` vanishes\" — it\n*determines* the neutral slot uniquely. This is the precise missing object the\nprior result and the U(1)-assignment audit named\n(`docs/audits/2026-06-02-u1-hypercharge-assignment.md`: \"the precise missing\nobject is a SECOND, independent crossing invariant (a baryon-number / color-trace\ncharge)\"). The corpus does **not** supply such an `S` for the same-sign even-twist\ntriple; this conditional makes \"fixed only by the second-charge / mixing data\"\nprecise. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.signed_which_slot_is_W_free","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.signed_which_slot_is_W_free","kind":"theorem","line":595,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L595-L607","doc":"**The signed / C-invariance criterion does NOT force which slot is `W`.** Both\n`signedWat4` (paper: `W` chiral at slot 4, `Z` amphichiral at slot 6) and\n`signedWat6` (mirror) are valid `SignedEWLabeling`s satisfying the full\ncharge-conjugation neutrality constraint, yet they disagree on the charged slot\n(`sw 4 = 2` vs `sw 4 = 0`). Admitting the *signed* `σ ↔ σ⁻¹` asymmetry — the first\ningredient the prior result named — therefore leaves ≥ 2 labelings consistent: it\nconstrains the neutral slot to be **amphichiral**, but not **which** slot. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.signedWat6","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.signedWat6","kind":"def","line":589,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L589-L593","doc":"The mirror signed labeling: neutral at slot `4`, charged `W` (chiral,\n`sw = 2`) at slot `6`. Equally C-consistent. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.signedWat4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.signedWat4","kind":"def","line":583,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L583-L587","doc":"The paper's signed labeling: charged `W` (chiral, `sw = 2`) at slot `4`,\nneutral `Z`/`W³` (amphichiral, `sw = 0`) at slot `6`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.SignedEWLabeling.neutral_at_4_xor_6","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.SignedEWLabeling.neutral_at_4_xor_6","kind":"theorem","line":580,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L580-L580","doc":"Exactly one vector slot is C-invariant (neutral); the other is chiral. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.SignedEWLabeling.sw","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.SignedEWLabeling.sw","kind":"def","line":578,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L578-L578","doc":"Signed writhe at each vector-slot crossing count. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.SignedEWLabeling.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.SignedEWLabeling.mk","kind":"ctor","line":576,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L576-L576","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.SignedEWLabeling","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.SignedEWLabeling","kind":"structure","line":570,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L570-L581","doc":"A **signed** crossing→charge labeling of the two vector slots (crossing counts\n`4` and `6`): each slot carries a signed writhe, and — by\n`cInvariant_iff_writhe_zero` — the **neutral** slot is the C-invariant one\n(`sw = 0`) and the **charged** slot the chiral one (`sw ≠ 0`). A valid electroweak\nlabeling makes exactly one vector slot neutral (the `Z`/`W³`) and the other\ncharged (the `W`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.evenTwist_not_cInvariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.evenTwist_not_cInvariant","kind":"theorem","line":560,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L560-L568","doc":"**No pure even-twist carrier is C-invariant / amphichiral.** For `k ≥ 1` the\nsigned writhe `2k ≠ 0`, so `C` never fixes it: the all-positive braid `σ₁^{2k}` is\ngenuinely chiral. Hence **no pure even-twist slot** can be the neutral (C-fixed)\nelectroweak member. The proof genuinely runs `cInvariant_iff_writhe_zero` against\n`2k ≠ 0` — it is not vacuous. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.evenTwistSignedWrithe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.evenTwistSignedWrithe","kind":"def","line":555,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L555-L558","doc":"**Signed** writhe of the pure even-twist carrier `T(2,2k) = σ₁^{2k}`: `+2k`\n(all crossings positive). Same value as `evenTwistWrithe`, restated in the signed\nlayer. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.cInvariant_iff_writhe_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.cInvariant_iff_writhe_zero","kind":"theorem","line":547,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L547-L553","doc":"**C-invariance ⟺ amphichirality ⟺ zero signed writhe.** A carrier is a fixed\npoint of charge conjugation (its own antiparticle — the neutrality criterion of\n`chirality-trefoil`) exactly when its signed writhe vanishes. Over `ℤ` the content\nis `−w = w ↔ 2w = 0 ↔ w = 0` — the load-bearing step (`omega`), *not* a type\ntautology. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.crossingReversal_involutive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.crossingReversal_involutive","kind":"theorem","line":541,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L541-L545","doc":"`C` is an involution (`σ² = id`), matching the fibre-adjoint involution of\n`chirality-trefoil`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.crossingReversal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.crossingReversal","kind":"def","line":536,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L536-L539","doc":"Charge conjugation `C` on the signed writhe: crossing reversal `σ ↔ σ⁻¹`\nnegates every crossing sign, hence negates the writhe (`predicted-spectra/\nchirality-trefoil-electron-positron`: `Q(𝔭^σ) = −Q(𝔭)`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.writheI3_does_not_select_neutral_slot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.writheI3_does_not_select_neutral_slot","kind":"theorem","line":487,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L487-L513","doc":"**The surviving `writhe → I₃` map is INCOMPATIBLE with any valid electroweak\nlabeling** (the non-vacuous negative result). Two facts do the work:\n\n* the writhe-derived doubled isospin is **nonzero on every carrier** — `2·I₃(σ₁⁴)\n  = 4 ≠ 0`, `2·I₃(σ₃⁶) = 6 ≠ 0`, `2·I₃(σ₅⁸) = 8 ≠ 0` (the all-positive braids\n  have no zero-writhe slot);\n* every valid `EWVectorLabeling` **requires** a neutral (`t3 = 0`) vector slot\n  (`has_neutral_slot`) — the `Z`.\n\nSince the writhe map never produces the required `0`, **no** valid labeling can\nagree with it on the two vector slots. The proof genuinely uses the nonzeroness\nof the writhe assignment against the labeling's mandatory neutral slot — it is\n*not* true by the `t3 ∈ {0,1}` type constraint alone. Hence the one\ncrossing→quantum-number map that survives the U(1)-assignment audit assigns\n*all* carriers a nonzero isospin and so **cannot select the neutral `Z` slot**;\nwhich-slot-is-`W` remains a **free label**, strengthening rather than closing\n`which_slot_is_W_free`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWVectorLabeling.has_neutral_slot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWVectorLabeling.has_neutral_slot","kind":"theorem","line":477,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L477-L485","doc":"**Every valid `EWVectorLabeling` has a neutral vector slot.** The\n`charged_at_4_xor_6` datum puts the charge (`t3 = 1`) on exactly one of the two\nvector slots, so the *other* slot is neutral (`t3 = 0`) — this is the `Z`. Any\nelectroweak labeling therefore *requires* one of `{σ₁⁴, σ₃⁶}` to carry `t3 = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.evenTwist_doubledI3_strictMono","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.evenTwist_doubledI3_strictMono","kind":"theorem","line":468,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L468-L475","doc":"**`writhe → I₃` is a monotone twist ladder, not a sign charge.** Across the\ncarriers it strictly increases (`k = 2 ↦ 4 < k = 3 ↦ 6 < k = 4 ↦ 8`) with no sign\nchange and no zero — the signature of a magnitude / spin ladder (audit §3), not\nof an additive charge. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.evenTwist_doubledI3_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.evenTwist_doubledI3_pos","kind":"theorem","line":462,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L462-L466","doc":"**The surviving `writhe → I₃` map assigns strictly positive isospin to every\neven-twist carrier.** In particular both vector slots `k = 2` (σ₁⁴) and `k = 3`\n(σ₃⁶) get `2·I₃ > 0` — neither is neutral. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.evenTwistDoubledI3_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.evenTwistDoubledI3_eq","kind":"theorem","line":460,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L460-L460","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.evenTwistDoubledI3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.evenTwistDoubledI3","kind":"def","line":455,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L455-L458","doc":"Doubled isospin `2·I₃` assigned by the surviving audit map `writhe → I₃`\n(`2·I₃ = writhe`) to the even-twist carrier `T(2, 2k)`. Since the carrier is the\nall-positive braid `σ₁^{2k}` (writhe `2k`), this equals `2k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.evenTwistWrithe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.evenTwistWrithe","kind":"def","line":450,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L450-L453","doc":"Writhe of the all-positive even-twist torus link `T(2, 2k)` = closure of the\npositive braid `σ₁^{2k}`: `2k` positive crossings, no negative crossings, so\n`w = n₊ − n₋ = 2k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.which_slot_is_W_free","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.which_slot_is_W_free","kind":"theorem","line":401,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L401-L417","doc":"**Which slot is `W` is UNDETERMINED (a free label).** Both `labelWat4` (the\npaper's `W = σ₁⁴`) and `labelWat6` (`W = σ₃⁶`) are valid `EWVectorLabeling`s and\nthey disagree on the charged slot (`t3 4 = 1` vs `t3 4 = 0`). No *proved*\ncrossing→charge principle selects between them: the corpus `writhe → Q` map\n(`Q = ½·writhe`) makes *every* even-twist carrier charged (`Q = k`), and\n`writhe → Y` is falsified. Hence `W = σ₁⁴` is a labeling choice — supported by\nthe mass ordering `4 < 6 < 8` (necessary, not sufficient) — and **not** a\ntheorem. What *would* force it is a genuine crossing/linking → `T₃` (or electric\ncharge) map assigning the neutral label to exactly the `Z` slot; the corpus does\nnot yet supply one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.labelWat6","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.labelWat6","kind":"def","line":395,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L395-L399","doc":"The mirror labeling: charged `W` at the 6-crossing slot `σ₃⁶`, neutral at\n`σ₁⁴`. Equally admissible under the proved constraints. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.labelWat4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.labelWat4","kind":"def","line":389,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L389-L393","doc":"The paper's labeling: charged `W` at the 4-crossing slot `σ₁⁴`, neutral `Z`\nat the 6-crossing slot `σ₃⁶`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWVectorLabeling.charged_at_4_xor_6","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWVectorLabeling.charged_at_4_xor_6","kind":"theorem","line":387,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L387-L387","doc":"Exactly one of the two vector slots (`4` or `6`) carries the charge. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWVectorLabeling.t3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWVectorLabeling.t3","kind":"def","line":385,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L385-L385","doc":"Doubled isospin at each crossing count. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWVectorLabeling.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWVectorLabeling.mk","kind":"ctor","line":383,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L383-L383","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWVectorLabeling","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWVectorLabeling","kind":"structure","line":377,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L377-L387","doc":"A crossing→isospin labeling of the two *vector* (`A₋` doublet) electroweak\nslots, indexed by their crossing counts. `t3` gives the doubled isospin at each\nadmissible crossing count `4` (`σ₁⁴`) and `6` (`σ₃⁶`); a valid electroweak\nlabeling puts the charged carrier (`|t3| = 1`) on exactly one of the two slots\nand the neutral carrier (`t3 = 0`) on the other. Nothing in the proved core\ndistinguishes the two ways of doing this. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.charged_are_doublets_singlet_neutral","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.charged_are_doublets_singlet_neutral","kind":"theorem","line":360,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L360-L375","doc":"**Forced part of the charge labeling.** From the sector postulate alone: the\ncharged carriers `W±` (`t₃ = ±1 ≠ 0`) are bar-odd `A₋` doublets, and the `A₊`\nsinglet `H` is neutral (`t₃ = 0`). So *charge ⇒ doublet* and *singlet ⇒ neutral*\nhold for these carriers. What is **not** entailed is which crossing slot the\ncharged pair occupies — that is the free label of `which_slot_is_W_free`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.ew_sigma5_bargrade_forced","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.ew_sigma5_bargrade_forced","kind":"theorem","line":333,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L333-L343","doc":"**σ₅⁸ bar-grading FORCED by spin (Task 2 — derived, not stated).** Given only\nthe physical spins, the Higgs (scalar, `2s = 0`) is forced into `A₊` (bar-even\nsinglet) and the hypercharge boson `B` (vector, `2s = 2`) into `A₋` (bar-odd\ndoublet), through the same spin↔sector inversion (`barSectorOfSpin`,\n`barSectorOfSpin_inverts`) that governs the whole triplet. The σ₅⁸ H/B grading\nis therefore a *consequence* of the two carriers' spins, not an owner postulate;\nthe single residual postulate is that both `H` and `B` occupy the one σ₅⁸ slot. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.spin58","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.spin58","kind":"def","line":326,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L326-L331","doc":"Physical (Standard-Model measured) doubled spin of each σ₅⁸ occupant: the\nHiggs is a scalar (`2s = 0`), the hypercharge boson `B` is a vector (`2s = 2`).\nThese are independent physical inputs, **not** sector assignments. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.instDecidableEqSigma58","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.instDecidableEqSigma58","kind":"instance","line":324,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L324-L324","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.Sigma58.hyperB","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.Sigma58.hyperB","kind":"ctor","line":323,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L323-L323","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.Sigma58.higgs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.Sigma58.higgs","kind":"ctor","line":322,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L322-L322","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.Sigma58","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.Sigma58","kind":"inductive","line":317,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L317-L324","doc":"The two occupants of the Hoefsmit slot `σ₅⁸` (`= T(2,8)`, strands 5–6): the\nHiggs boson `H` and the `U(1)_Y` hypercharge gauge boson `B`. The residual\nsector postulate is *only* that both inhabit this one slot; their bar-sectors\nare DERIVED from spin below. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.barSectorOfSpin_inverts","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.barSectorOfSpin_inverts","kind":"theorem","line":308,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L308-L315","doc":"**`barSectorOfSpin` is a genuine two-sided inverse of the spin grading.** For\nevery EW carrier it recovers the sector from the spin (`barSectorOfSpin ∘\nspinDouble = isSinglet`). This injectivity is what makes \"spin forces sector\" a\n*derivation* rather than a re-postulation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.barSectorOfSpin","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.barSectorOfSpin","kind":"def","line":303,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L303-L306","doc":"Bar-sector recovered from the (doubled) spin via the spin-involution grading\nlaw of `def:spin-involution`: `A₊` (bar-even singlet) `⟺ 2s = 0`, `A₋` (bar-odd\ndoublet) `⟺ 2s = 2`. `true = A₊`, `false = A₋`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.sector_forced_by_spin","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.sector_forced_by_spin","kind":"theorem","line":292,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L292-L301","doc":"**Spin forces the sector (the injective inverse of `spinDouble`).** A scalar\n(`spinDouble c = 0`) must inhabit the singlet `A₊` (`isSinglet = true`); a vector\n(`spinDouble c = 2`) must inhabit the doublet `A₋` (`isSinglet = false`). The\nsector is *determined* by the spin — it is not an independent free choice once\nthe spin is fixed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.ew_charge_spin_forced","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.ew_charge_spin_forced","kind":"theorem","line":257,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L257-L279","doc":"**Theorem (charge + spin forced from the selection postulate).**\n\nConditional on the single physics postulate `EWSectorSelection`, the full\nspin and isospin table of the electroweak triplet is *derived*: `H` is a\nneutral scalar, `W±` are charged vectors with `T₃ = ±1`, `Z` is a\n(mixing-)neutral vector with `T₃ = 0`. C3 (charge) and C4 (spin) are no\nlonger independent open conjectures — they follow from the sector map and\nbar-parity. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:thm:ew-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution","label":"thm:ew-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution","md":"quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.wPlus_charged","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.wPlus_charged","kind":"theorem","line":253,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L253-L255","doc":"**`W⁺` is charged** — bar-odd doublet, not neutral. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.higgs_neutral","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.higgs_neutral","kind":"theorem","line":249,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L249-L251","doc":"**Higgs is neutral** — bar-even singlet. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.z_vector","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.z_vector","kind":"theorem","line":245,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L245-L247","doc":"**`Z` is a vector** (`spin 1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.wMinus_vector","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.wMinus_vector","kind":"theorem","line":241,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L241-L243","doc":"**`W⁻` is a vector** (`spin 1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.wPlus_vector","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.wPlus_vector","kind":"theorem","line":237,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L237-L239","doc":"**`W⁺` is a vector** (`spin 1`) — forced by the doublet postulate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.higgs_scalar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.higgs_scalar","kind":"theorem","line":233,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L233-L235","doc":"**Higgs is a scalar** (`spin 0`) — forced by the singlet postulate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.isNeutralByParity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.isNeutralByParity","kind":"def","line":229,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L229-L231","doc":"**Neutrality** (bar-even membership): singlet carriers are neutral. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.spinDouble","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.spinDouble","kind":"def","line":224,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L224-L227","doc":"**Doubled spin** (`2s`), *defined* from the sector: singlet `⇒ 0` (scalar,\nspin 0), doublet `⇒ 2` (vector, spin 1). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWSectorSelection.higgs_t3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWSectorSelection.higgs_t3","kind":"theorem","line":220,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L220-L220","doc":"Higgs: `T₃ = 0` — neutral singlet. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWSectorSelection.z_t3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWSectorSelection.z_t3","kind":"theorem","line":218,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L218-L218","doc":"`Z`: `T₃ = 0` — neutral via Weinberg mixing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWSectorSelection.wMinus_t3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWSectorSelection.wMinus_t3","kind":"theorem","line":216,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L216-L216","doc":"`W⁻`: `T₃ = −1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWSectorSelection.wPlus_t3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWSectorSelection.wPlus_t3","kind":"theorem","line":214,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L214-L214","doc":"`W⁺`: `T₃ = +1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWSectorSelection.t3Double","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWSectorSelection.t3Double","kind":"def","line":212,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L212-L212","doc":"Doubled isospin `2·T₃` label map. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWSectorSelection.z_doublet","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWSectorSelection.z_doublet","kind":"theorem","line":210,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L210-L210","doc":"`Z` is a bar-odd doublet (vector); neutral via mixing, not via `A₊`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWSectorSelection.wMinus_doublet","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWSectorSelection.wMinus_doublet","kind":"theorem","line":208,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L208-L208","doc":"`W⁻` is a bar-odd doublet. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWSectorSelection.wPlus_doublet","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWSectorSelection.wPlus_doublet","kind":"theorem","line":206,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L206-L206","doc":"`W⁺` is a bar-odd doublet. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWSectorSelection.higgs_singlet","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWSectorSelection.higgs_singlet","kind":"theorem","line":204,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L204-L204","doc":"Higgs is the bar-even self-dual singlet. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWSectorSelection.isSinglet","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWSectorSelection.isSinglet","kind":"def","line":202,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L202-L202","doc":"`true` = spin-singlet (`A₊`); `false` = spin-doublet (`A₋`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWSectorSelection.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWSectorSelection.mk","kind":"ctor","line":200,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L200-L200","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWSectorSelection","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWSectorSelection","kind":"class","line":191,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L191-L220","doc":"**The single physics selection postulate** (axiomatised `def:spin-involution`\nsector map + bare `T₃` label). Content-bearing §3b conjecture class: it fixes\nwhich carrier is a spin-singlet (`A₊`, bar-even, neutral) versus a spin-doublet\n(`A₋`, bar-odd, charged), and the isospin labels. Everything else is derived.\n\nThe Higgs is the singlet (`self-dual-higgs-real-volume`); `W±, Z` are doublets.\nThe `Z ↦ 0` label is neutral *via the Weinberg `(W³,B) → (Z,γ)` mixing*\n(`weinberg-angle-categorical`), not by bar-even membership — the one residual\nsubtlety carried explicitly. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.instDecidableEqEWCarrier","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.instDecidableEqEWCarrier","kind":"instance","line":189,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L189-L189","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWCarrier.H","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWCarrier.H","kind":"ctor","line":188,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L188-L188","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWCarrier.Z","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWCarrier.Z","kind":"ctor","line":187,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L187-L187","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWCarrier.Wm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWCarrier.Wm","kind":"ctor","line":186,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L186-L186","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWCarrier.Wp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWCarrier.Wp","kind":"ctor","line":185,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L185-L185","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWCarrier","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWCarrier","kind":"inductive","line":183,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L183-L189","doc":"The four electroweak carriers. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.skew_minusPart_carrier","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.skew_minusPart_carrier","kind":"theorem","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L163-L172","doc":"**Bar-odd (charged) value.** The skew (`P_skew`) functional of the bar-odd\npart is `q^{2k} − q^{-2k}` (`= 2sinh`) — nonzero exactly when `a² ≠ 1`, i.e.\nthe carrier is genuinely charged. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.trSum_minusPart_carrier","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.trSum_minusPart_carrier","kind":"theorem","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L154-L161","doc":"**Bar-odd (charged) channel is traceless.** The charged (`P_skew`) part\ncarries zero Markov trace — the neutrality of the trace on the charged sector. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.trSum_plusPart_carrier","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.trSum_plusPart_carrier","kind":"theorem","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L143-L151","doc":"**Bar-even (neutral) value.** The retained Markov trace of the bar-even\npart of the carrier is `q^{2k} + q^{-2k}` (`= 2cosh`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.plusPart_add_minusPart","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.plusPart_add_minusPart","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L134-L141","doc":"The spin decomposition on the block: `p = a₊ + a₋`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.swap₂_minusPart","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.swap₂_minusPart","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L126-L132","doc":"The bar-odd part is `σ`-negated (`∈ A₋`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.swap₂_plusPart","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.swap₂_plusPart","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L117-L123","doc":"The bar-even part is `σ`-fixed (`∈ A₊`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.swap₂_carrier","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.swap₂_carrier","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L112-L114","doc":"`swap₂` sends the carrier `(q^{2k}, q^{-2k})` to `(q^{-2k}, q^{2k})` — the\nbar image. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.carrier_snd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.carrier_snd","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L109-L109","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.carrier_fst","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.carrier_fst","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L107-L107","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.carrier","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.carrier","kind":"def","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L102-L104","doc":"The carrier of eigenvalue `a = q^{2k} ∈ Rˣ`: the pair\n`(q^{2k}, q^{-2k}) = (↑a, ↑a⁻¹)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.swap₂_involutive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.swap₂_involutive","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L99-L100","doc":"`swap₂` is an involution. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.minusPart","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.minusPart","kind":"def","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L95-L96","doc":"Bar-odd projection `a₋ = ½ (p − σ p)` on the block. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.plusPart","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.plusPart","kind":"def","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L92-L93","doc":"Bar-even projection `a₊ = ½ (p + σ p)` on the block. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.skew","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.skew","kind":"def","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L89-L90","doc":"Charge (skew / `P_skew`) functional: the bar-odd channel. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.trSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.trSum","kind":"def","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L86-L87","doc":"Neutral (Markov-trace) functional: the retained bar-even channel. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.swap₂","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.swap₂","kind":"def","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution.lean#L81-L84","doc":"The concrete spin involution on the sym/alt block: the **swap**\n`(x, y) ↦ (y, x)` — the bar involution `q^{2k} ↔ q^{-2k}` on the eigenvalue\npair. ","signatureChunk":0}]}